  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Les capacit&#xe9;s des Etats membres de ratifier et d&apos;appliquer les normes internationales du travail ainsi que de  s&apos;acquitter de leurs obligations en mati&#xe8;re de pr&#xe9;sentation de rapports  sont renforc&#xe9;es</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The &#x201d;Trade for Decent Work&#x201d; project is a global project aimed at improving the application of the fundamental ILO Conventions in countries that are trade partners of the European Union, and includes the promotion of the ILO Tripartite Declaration of Principles on Multinational Enterprises and Social Policy. More information on the project is available at: https://www.ilo.org/global/standards/WCMS_697996/lang--en/index.htm. The implementation of the project in Cabo Verde follows a logic of continuity, builds on the results of the project &quot;Support for the Effective Implementation of International Labour Standards under the GSP+&quot; and will contribute to the three drivers of cross-cutting policies that are International Labour Standards, Social Dialogue and Gender Equality and Non-discrimination.
RATIFICATION OF fundamental and governance Conventions or Protocols (Output 1.1.1)
-	Gap analysis on the Protocol to the Forced Labour Convention, 1930 (done);
-	Process of ratification ongoing. To be accomplished in December 2024.
APPLICATION OF RATIFIED ILO CONVENTIONS (Output1.2)
-	Revision of the Labour Code (consultant hired)
-	List of hazardous types of work prohibited to children in line with ILO conventions to be adopted
-	Study on trafficking of persons (done)</narrative>
  </description>
